---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { repoBlob } from "../../lib/links.mjs";
---

<DocsLayout title="Skills — sum">
  <div class="doc">
    <h1>Skills</h1>
    <p class="lede">Four procedures keep action-specific detail out of the shared entry contract. Read AGENTS.md and the procedure for the current action.</p>
<div class="kv lg" style="grid-template-columns:160px 1fr"><div class="k">/sum-work</div><div class="v">Implement directly or brief, launch, steer, and wait for bounded helpers. <a href={repoBlob("skills/sum-work/SKILL.md")}> Work ↗</a></div><div class="k">/sum-review</div><div class="v">Inspect a specified stable candidate independently; save findings and send them to the immediate parent. <a href={repoBlob("skills/sum-review/SKILL.md")}> Review ↗</a></div><div class="k">/sum-finish</div><div class="v">Account for required checks and findings, deliver within authority, and clean up conservatively. <a href={repoBlob("skills/sum-finish/SKILL.md")}> Finish ↗</a></div><div class="k">/sum-resume</div><div class="v">Inspect actual work, reports, and recipients after interruption before continuing. <a href={repoBlob("skills/sum-resume/SKILL.md")}> Resume ↗</a></div></div><div class="sec">
<h2>Discovery and briefs</h2>
<p>The <code>.agents/skills/</code> and <code>.claude/skills/</code> links expose the same four procedures. Harness pointer files load the shared entry contract; a pointer is not harness qualification.</p><p>Helpers working in another repository receive the absolute readable procedure path in their brief. Keep that instruction checkout available until those helpers finish.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Optional development tools</h2>
<p>Portable verification and evidence authoring tools under <code>.agents/skills/</code> are optional repository development tools. They are not ordinary startup requirements.</p><p><a href={repoBlob("CONTRIBUTING.md")}> Development guide ↗</a></p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Separate legacy products</h2>
<p>The Grok Bot packs retain their Bot messaging and Cursor Cloud Agent delegation. Their software-factory lane requires its separately preserved compatible legacy installation. The four native HC procedures do not replace that lane.</p><p><a href={repoBlob("docs/legacy.md")}> Legacy product boundary ↗</a></p>
</div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
